 "notes_en": [
  "Fair sentries: once the knight picks up the stone, he waits for the right moment and walks behind the sentry’s back, not right next to him. A sentry always notices the knight in a neighbouring cell. Without the stone the knight goes at once, and the sentries keep walking as they were."
